{"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"patch":0,"minor":3},"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"Overview","text":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/Trie","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" is a set of sequences and a "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/TrieDictionary","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" a dictionary keyed by them, both kept in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"a trie (Fredkin, 1960): a tree whose edges carry symbols and whose root-to-vertex paths spell the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"keys. They answer the queries a hash set cannot: every key with a prefix"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"("},{"code":"elements(withPrefix:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", whose "},{"code":"count","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is O(1)), whether any key has one ("},{"code":"hasPrefix(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"), and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the longest key that is a prefix of a query ("},{"code":"longestPrefix(of:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":")."}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["import Tries","","let words = Trie([\"car\", \"cart\", \"cat\", \"dog\"])","words.contains(\"cat\")                                   \/\/ true","words.elements(withPrefix: \"car\").map { String($0) }    \/\/ [\"car\", \"cart\"]","words.longestPrefix(of: \"carton\").map { String($0) }    \/\/ \"cart\""]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Keys are any sequence of the symbol type and are stored as "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"[Symbol]"},{"type":"text","text":". For text, the symbol"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"type decides what a step is: "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Trie<Character>"},{"type":"text","text":" steps by grapheme cluster, "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Trie<Unicode.Scalar>"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"by scalar, and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Trie<UInt8>"},{"type":"text","text":" over "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"utf8"},{"type":"text","text":" by byte, the fastest of the three, because comparing"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"bytes is cheaper than comparing "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Character"},{"type":"text","text":"s. When the symbols are "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Comparable"},{"type":"text","text":", each vertex keeps"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"its children sorted, so iteration is in lexicographic order; otherwise children come in the order"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"they were added."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/RadixTree","isActive":true},{"text":" and a ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/RadixTreeDictionary","isActive":true},{"text":" hold the same keys and answer the same queries,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"with the same names, in a radix tree (Morrison, 1968): every chain of vertices with one child and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"no key is merged into one edge labelled with all its symbols, so there is a vertex per key and per","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"branching point rather than per symbol. They suit keys with long shared prefixes, such as file","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"paths or URLs, and build faster and in less memory than a trie of the same keys.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A trie’s shape converts to Grafluent’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"PrefixTree"},{"type":"text","text":" with "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"PrefixTree(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":", and a radix tree’s to"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"an "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Arborescence"},{"type":"text","text":" of its vertices’ prefixes with "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Arborescence(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":" (import Grafluent’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Trees"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"module beside this one)."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"An "},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/AhoCorasickAutomaton","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" (Aho and Corasick, 1975) finds every occurrence of any of a set of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"patterns in one pass over a text, in O("},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"n"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"type":"text","text":" + "},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"z"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"type":"text","text":") for "},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"n","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"type":"text","text":" symbols and "},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"z","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"type":"text","text":" matches: a trie of the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"patterns with failure links. Its "},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/AhoCorasickAutomaton\/statesView-swift.property","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" is the automaton as a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"DirectedGraph","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["let automaton = AhoCorasickAutomaton(patterns: [\"he\", \"she\", \"his\", \"hers\"])","automaton.matches(in: \"ushers\").map(\\.patternIndex)   \/\/ [1, 0, 3]"]}],"kind":"content"}],"metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"Tries"}],"role":"collection","roleHeading":"Framework","title":"Tries","symbolKind":"module","externalID":"Tries"},"sections":[],"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"Tries over sequences of any ","type":"text"},{"code":"Hashable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" symbols, with prefix queries, and multi-pattern matching.","type":"text"}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/tries"]}],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[[]]},"topicSections":[{"title":"Sets of sequences","anchor":"Sets-of-sequences","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/Trie","doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/RadixTree"]},{"title":"Dictionaries keyed by sequences","anchor":"Dictionaries-keyed-by-sequences","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/TrieDictionary","doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/RadixTreeDictionary"]},{"title":"Pattern matching","anchor":"Pattern-matching","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/AhoCorasickAutomaton"]},{"generated":true,"title":"Extended Modules","anchor":"Extended-Modules","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/Trees"]}],"references":{"doc://Tries/documentation/Tries/AhoCorasickAutomaton/statesView-swift.property":{"role":"symbol","conformance":{"constraints":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Symbol"},{"type":"text","text":" conforms to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Hashable"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"availabilityPrefix":[{"type":"text","text":"Available when"}],"conformancePrefix":[{"type":"text","text":"Conforms when"}]},"type":"topic","title":"statesView","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"var"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"statesView"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"AhoCorasickAutomaton","preciseIdentifier":"s:5Tries20AhoCorasickAutomatonV"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Symbol"},{"kind":"text","text":">."},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"StatesView","preciseIdentifier":"s:5Tries20AhoCorasickAutomatonV10StatesViewV"}],"url":"\/documentation\/tries\/ahocorasickautomaton\/statesview-swift.property","abstract":[{"text":"The automaton’s states as a directed graph: a vertex per state, numbered from 0 for the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"root, a goto edge from each state to each of its trie children, and a failure edge from","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"each state but the root to its failure state. ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/AhoCorasickAutomaton\/StatesView-swift.struct\/symbol(ofEdgeAt:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" tells the two","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"apart.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/AhoCorasickAutomaton\/statesView-swift.property"},"doc://Tries/documentation/Tries":{"type":"topic","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Tries over sequences of any "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Hashable"},{"type":"text","text":" symbols, with prefix queries, and multi-pattern matching."}],"role":"collection","url":"\/documentation\/tries","title":"Tries","identifier":"doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries"},"doc://Tries/documentation/Tries/RadixTreeDictionary":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/RadixTreeDictionary","type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"A dictionary keyed by sequences, kept in a radix tree (Morrison, 1968): a trie in which every","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"chain of vertices with one child and no key is merged into one edge labelled with all its","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"symbols, each key’s vertex holding its value.","type":"text"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"RadixTreeDictionary","kind":"identifier"}],"role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/tries\/radixtreedictionary","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"RadixTreeDictionary","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol","title":"RadixTreeDictionary"},"doc://Tries/documentatio